{"name":"Boyzone","hex":"#2a96d5","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[],"entries":[{"title":"Boyzone","blocks":[{"text":"Boyzone are an Irish boy band created in 1993 by the talent manager Louis Walsh. Before even recording any material, Boyzone made an appearance on RTÉ's The Late Late Show. Its most successful line-up was composed of Keith Duffy, Stephen Gately, Mikey Graham, Ronan Keating, and Shane Lynch. As of 2018, Boyzone had released seven studio albums and nine compilation albums."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/65/Boyzone.jpg/330px-Boyzone.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Boyzone","wikidata":"Q213495"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c5/Louiswalsh.jpg/330px-Louiswalsh.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c5/Louiswalsh.jpg/330px-Louiswalsh.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Music manager Louis Walsh wished to create an \"Irish version of Take That\"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ALouiswalsh.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8b/RonanKeating.jpg/500px-RonanKeating.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8b/RonanKeating.jpg/1280px-RonanKeating.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8b/RonanKeating.jpg/500px-RonanKeating.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Lead singer Ronan Keating, 2002","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ARonanKeating.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b2/Boyzonetour2009.jpg/330px-Boyzonetour2009.jpg?utm